    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n43640" root="&#xA;                        مطى&#xA;                    " body-key="m1">
                        
                            1
                            <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مَطَا</span></b> 
                         signifies <i>He drew,</i> or <i>pulled,</i> a thing;
as, for instance, a well-rope: for] <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مَدٌّ</span> and <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مَطٌّ</span>
and <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مَطْوٌ</span> are all one. (Az and TA in art. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مط</span>.) See
an ex. from Zuheyr, voce <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">ثِنَايَةٌ</span>.

